}], "source": "$$\n(H1) + (H2) + (H3)\n\\Rightarrow\n\\text{ there exists a versal formal object}\n$$", "source_byte_span": {"end": 504, "start": 424}, "source_hash": "sha256:49a50c574f6eb4854457e94d4c3cecfb73cb65c413c7c242fd904a0864567bb5"}], "node_kind": "remark", "parent_tag": "06SX", "placeholders": {"LOCKED_0001": "\\label{remark-compare-schlessinger-H3-pre}", "MATHSEG_0001": "$$\n(H1) + (H2) + (H3)\n\\Rightarrow\n\\text{", "MATHSEG_0002": "}\n$$", "MATH_0001": "$F : \\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda \\to \\textit{Sets}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\dim_k TF < \\infty$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{remark-compare-S1-S2-schlessinger}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-versal-object-existence}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{remark-compare-schlessinger-H3}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{remark}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\end{remark}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 2, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:124526b1cd01d6f5586ffb7ddc3e2bd937def76ac44e557d3565b1f7c5810eeb", "source_math_skeleton_hash": "sha256:8ecacb333e72191e7c1487bb26b6a43f70a06aa7b0694b81444a599b9775f6cb", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:723e09fac2e39a11b6a8249f17a2fb1d53edf7ba3cdfc4142a71f9a9eb19bedf", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\n<LOCKED_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a predeformation functor\nsatisfying (S1) and (S2). The condition <MATH_0002>\nis precisely condition (H3) from Schlessinger's paper.\nRecall that (S1) and (S2) correspond to conditions (H1) and (H2), see\nRemark <REF_0001>.\nThus Lemma <REF_0002> tells us\n<MATHSEG_0001> there exists a versal formal object<MATHSEG_0002>\nfor predeformation functors. We will make the link with hulls in\nRemark <REF_0003>.\n<STRUCT_0002>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:dbfa9456e3f5281112d6285d3bc15abd56959433737b73f264b4770d9226b0d3", "unit_id": "inventory:formal-defos:0D3G:remark/0001"}}}, {"context_id": "locked-English-neighbor:formal-defos:inventory:formal-defos:06T0:paragraph/0001", "hash": "sha256:b3464612d6db4b4a41c2e82eadf415a8c34515a3c4ae9eeb884e5dc58ed3958a", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-neighbor", "location": {"byte_end": 156291, "byte_start": 155915, "file": "formal-defos.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:a707a32688c57392285c8ee907dfbc161ecc25c97158aa811016feae3bbb9e9c", "line_end": 4072, "line_start": 4066}, "owner_tag": "06T0", "parent_tag": "06T0", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "06T0", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:1b4675bcab0e1704eb15dd5abdaecaafd97954466fd75b2ec5b3a2ebdf495b05", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nWe do a little bit of work to try and understand (non)uniqueness\nof versal formal objects. It turns out that if a predeformation category\nhas a versal formal object, then it has a minimal versal formal\nobject and any two such are isomorphic. Moreover, all versal formal\nobjects are ``more or less'' the same up to replacing the base ring\nby a power series extension.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:277592b6bcd8da55dded3e104e2ab200a79102ff0fb51d5ea94e5b4dbf35975c", "unit_id": "inventory:formal-defos:06T0:paragraph/0001"}}}], "input_freeze": {"hash": "sha256:1e3a17b333c5af2c0127d7db4943a71f54dd5f80daebd286e0d2cd83c6fab8eb", "path": "translation-data/source-adoption-inputs/formal-defos90-gpt61sol-p018-r03-20261117.json"}, "model_output": {"hash": "sha256:82e1f770a33d052fab57ebe9425244709f070f3428e6c50e0578ca9e661ba301", "path": "docs/evidence/formal-defos90-gpt61sol-p018-r03-20261117-raw-01.jsonl", "record_hash": "sha256:b07fe75659b1536c626e2845384f05e87b25a2d42062dd70cabb02c4c049a713"}, "neighbor_unit_ids": 